# Copy this file to .env — .env itself is gitignored and must never be committed.
# The repo must run end-to-end with the defaults below and no API key.

LLM_PROVIDER=mock

# Required only when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic. Leave unset to run fully on MockProvider.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional. Pre-seeds each agent's expected image digest for identity/issuer.py's attestation
# check (AGENTFW_CONTEXT.md §2). Digest pinning itself is NOT optional and does not depend on
# these being set — identity now pins whichever digest it observes on an agent's first successful
# attestation (trust-on-first-use) and refuses every later attestation that doesn't match. Setting
# a var here just tells identity what to pin *before* trusting anything it observes, so the first
# real attestation is checked against a known-good value instead of blindly trusted. Leave unset
# and a fresh clone still gets real protection — it just starts from the first successful attest
# instead of a pre-verified one.
#
# IMPORTANT — this is the file most people get wrong here: edit `.env` (the file `cp .env.example
# .env` creates), not this one. Compose reads variables from `.env`; it never reads
# `.env.example` for substitution, so anything set only in this file has no effect at all. And
# make sure the line in `.env` has NO leading `#` — a commented-out line is the same as unset.
#
# To get the real digest, after `docker compose build`:
#   docker inspect $(docker compose images -q agent) --format '{{.Id}}'
# then, in `.env` (not here):
# EXPECTED_DIGEST_AGENT=sha256:...
# EXPECTED_DIGEST_FINANCE_AGENT=sha256:...
# EXPECTED_DIGEST_SUPPORT_AGENT=sha256:...
